# =============================================================================
# Nuxel Tor configuration (client only) - installed as /etc/tor/torrc
# =============================================================================
# Design decisions, and why they are the honest ones:
#
#  * CLIENT ONLY. There is no ExitRelay, no ORPort, no DirPort and no
#    relay/bridge role. A phone is not an exit node; this also keeps the
#    operator out of the abuse-report business.
#
#  * Loopback only for every port. SOCKS/DNS/TransPort/Control bind to
#    127.0.0.1 so that nothing on the network (and no app in a different
#    network namespace) can use the phone as an open proxy.
#
#  * ControlPort is enabled WITH CookieAuthentication and WITHOUT
#    HashedControlPassword. The cookie lives in /run/tor (tmpfs, 0640
#    debian-tor:debian-tor). This is what lets the privacy tool read real
#    circuit state (`GETINFO circuit-status`) instead of guessing from the
#    process being alive - "service running" and "circuit built" are different
#    claims and the UI must show both.
#
#  * DNSPort + AutomapHostsOnResolve: name resolution is meant to happen through
#    Tor, and the leak probe checks whether plaintext DNS still leaves the
#    device. A leak is REPORTED, never hidden.
#
#  * AvoidDiskWrites 1: flash longevity (a phone, not a server) and fewer
#    artefacts on disk.
#
#  * NO BRIDGES. No bridge lines, no pluggable transports are shipped. On a
#    censored network the owner adds them at /etc/tor/bridges.conf (see
#    tools/s10plus/a33/nuxel-vpn-tor.sh bridges-apply). Claiming censorship
#    resistance without shipping a transport would be a lie.
#
#  * SocksPolicy is loopback-only; a malicious local app still needs the
#    'network' capability grant to use the SOCKS port, and the socket itself is
#    owned by debian-tor with mode 0600 by default.

User debian-tor
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1
SocksPolicy reject *
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:9053
TransPort 127.0.0.1:9040
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1
CookieAuthFileGroupReadable 1
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1
VirtualAddrNetworkIPv4 10.192.0.0/10
AvoidDiskWrites 1
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log
# Exit relay: never.
ExitRelay 0
ExitPolicy reject *:*
# Relaying/bridging: never.
BridgeRelay 0
# An identifying nickname is not needed for a client and is one less thing to
# leak; deliberately unset.
